6.text:
The setup is competitive screening (multiple homeowners Bertrand-competing for scarce handymen), so any candidate menu must satisfy the agents' IR/IC constraints while yielding zero expected profit to each principal on every offered contract (i.e., \(p_i=v_i\)). Because \(\Pr(H)=5/6\) is large, any such candidate separating pair is vulnerable to a profitable pooling deviation that attracts both types and breaks even in expectation. Hence no separating equilibrium exists.

(The \(\theta\) feasibility bounds tighten \(v_L\le15\) but do not restore existence once competition is imposed.)

PUBLIC RESPONSE: {no separating eq. exists (high frac. H types => pooling deviation profitable)}

